abstract: |
  The India Water Canvas is a public-good commons-infrastructure artefact for
  India's water situation. It maps water Health (state of the water itself),
  Availability (quantity + delivery), and Impact (human + economic + climate
  consequence) at state and basin scale. It surfaces six self-reinforcing
  feedback loops driving water-system degradation; the funder ecosystem
  (~₹2.5–3.5 lakh crore/year government water spend); a ~₹3,000–5,000 crore/yr
  capture envelope (disbursement that does not produce its claimed outcome);
  and a phased civic-side build (~₹500–1,000 crore over 10 years) targeted at
  the highest-leverage Meadows points. The artefact is multi-audience by
  design — CSO, NGO, philanthropy, CSR, corporates, government, market
  entrants, journalists, citizens — with data routing rather than data
  forking. Written from the underlying 14-chapter prose folder.
